APS-016 — Policy Distribution

Document ID: APS-016
Title: Policy Distribution
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Policy Distribution Model (CPDM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Policy Distribution Model establishes the principles, architecture, governance, integrity mechanisms, and operational processes for securely distributing Canonical Policy Objects, Policy Packages, Policy Releases, and Policy Baselines throughout the Atlas ecosystem.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Distribution architecture
Distribution repositories
Distribution channels
Synchronization
Trust verification
Integrity validation
Update strategies
Distribution governance

This specification applies to every governed distribution of Atlas policy artifacts.

3. Canonical Definition

Policy Distribution is the governed process of securely delivering Canonical Policy Objects and related governance artifacts from authoritative repositories to authorized Atlas environments while preserving integrity, authenticity, traceability, and compatibility.

Distribution moves policy artifacts.

It SHALL NOT alter policy semantics.

4. Objectives

The Policy Distribution Model SHALL:

Preserve policy integrity.
Support trusted delivery.
Enable reproducible deployments.
Support federation.
Enable offline deployment.
Support synchronization.
Preserve governance.
Enable scalable distribution.
5. Distribution Principles

Every policy distribution SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Authenticity

Every distributed artifact SHALL originate from an authorized source.

Integrity

Every artifact SHALL be verified before installation.

Version Consistency

Distributed artifacts SHALL preserve declared versions.

Traceability

Every distribution SHALL be recorded.

Repeatability

Equivalent distribution requests SHALL produce equivalent artifact sets.

Governance

Distribution SHALL follow approved governance policies.

