7. Distribution Artifacts

Atlas recognizes the following distributable artifacts.

Artifact	Description
Policy Definition	Individual Canonical Policy Object
Policy Package	Deployable collection
Policy Release	Coordinated release
Policy Baseline	Effective governance state
Policy Vocabulary	Shared semantic definitions
Distribution Manifest	Installation metadata

Artifacts SHALL remain independently versioned.

8. Distribution Repositories

Atlas supports multiple repository types.

Repository	Purpose
Central Repository	Atlas authoritative source
Organization Repository	Internal governance
Domain Repository	Engineering discipline
Project Repository	Project-specific policies
Offline Repository	Disconnected deployment

Repositories SHALL expose immutable artifact identifiers.

9. Distribution Channels

Supported distribution channels include:

Secure API
Package transfer
Repository synchronization
Event-driven distribution
Scheduled updates
Offline media

Channels SHALL preserve authenticity and integrity.

10. Synchronization

Synchronization SHALL support:

Incremental updates
Full synchronization
Bidirectional federation
Conflict detection
Version reconciliation
Recovery after interruption

Synchronization SHALL NOT overwrite approved local governance without authorization.

11. Integrity Verification

Every distributed artifact SHALL be verified for:

Digital signature
Artifact checksum
Version compatibility
Dependency completeness
Manifest integrity
Trust chain validity

Verification SHALL precede installation.

12. Update Strategies

Atlas supports the following update strategies.

Strategy	Description
Immediate	Install immediately
Scheduled	Install at defined time
Manual	Administrator initiated
Phased	Incremental rollout
Canary	Limited deployment before general rollout
Emergency	Expedited governed deployment

The selected strategy SHALL be explicitly declared.

13. Distribution Lifecycle

Every distribution SHALL support:

Prepared
    │
Verified
    │
Distributed
    │
Installed
    │
Validated
    │
Activated
    │
Monitored

Every stage SHALL remain independently auditable.

14. Distribution Governance

Every distribution SHALL define:

Distribution authority
Source repository
Target environments
Applicable release
Applicable baseline
Approval requirements
Audit requirements

Governance SHALL accompany every distribution.

15. Distribution Quality

Every distribution SHALL satisfy:

Authenticity
Integrity
Completeness
Compatibility
Traceability
Recoverability
Auditability
Reproducibility

Quality SHALL be continuously monitored.

16. Conformance

A Policy Distribution implementation conforms if it:

Distributes canonical artifacts.
Verifies integrity.
Preserves version identity.
Supports synchronization.
Implements governed update strategies.
Maintains distribution traceability.
Preserves governance metadata.
17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Peer-to-peer policy distribution.
AI-assisted rollout planning.
Adaptive synchronization.
Blockchain-backed artifact verification.
Distributed policy registries.
Autonomous policy delivery networks.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical distribution semantics.

